Z||000001||btoth||04-20-2001||03:14 PM||||Keep this in mind when reinstalling Windows... the third time is the charm.  Windows likes to install differently every time you do it (sometimes it skips needed files, or set things up screwy, or doesn't detect things).  But, from my experiences with Windows... if you install it <B>3</B> times, it should be OK.  Well, as OK as Windows gets.<P>I bought Win2k because I was so sick of having to restart my computer for every little change and I was sick of Explorer errors trashing my whole system.  Win2k sure is nicer... but it has it's own quirks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||beer_stud_21||04-20-2001||03:51 PM||||Man, from a mac users standpoint this is the one thing that I cannot for the life of me figure out.  Why on earth can you people let yourselves be bent over a barrel by billy gates and his gang and yet not look for a better alternative.  I'm not saying you need to buy a mac, because I know there are lots of reasons people dont want to do that.  But Microsoft will always have a strangle hold on the computer world as long as the average joe refuses to try a different OS even though he is pulling his hair out trying to use a Microsoft product.  There are any number of linux's and even an OS called BeOS.  Its a great OS that is very powerfull and user friendly.  Nice interface and faster than a N* Fiero.  Only problem is it doesnt have a huge amount of apps for it.  But it does have basics like web browser, icq, etc.  There is even a free version you can download and install in windows just like it was another app.  No partitioning nessesary.  If you dont like it you can just uninstall it like any other app.<P>ok, im done...<BR>-Marlin||||reg||5
