Z||000004||btoth||04-20-2001||04:09 PM||||<B>beer_stud_21</B>:  What you say is so true, and I've been saying it for years.  <P>Unfortunately, there is never much of a selection of anything for the Mac... all the newest, greatest things come out for the PC and might eventually come to the Mac years later.  But, I can see why the developers don't bother with Macs too... there isn't the demand that there is for the Windows community.  It's an "evil circle" as I like to call it.  And I hope that things will change.<P>My solution:  Apple better get MacOS X ported to the PC so that I can build my cheap computers and not have to buy "Apple" brand everything... and they better find a way to run Windows software on top of MacOS X (kinda like how MacOS X can run OS 9 on top of it for old software).  Shouldn't be too hard to emulate the system commands of Windows if you're already running on a PC.  Then I could use the MacOS and still play my games, and since MacOS is UNIX based I could still do my UNIX programming that I need to do for college.  If I were CEO of Apple, I'd make it happen.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 04-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||04-20-2001||04:39 PM||||Dump Windows ME and go with Windows 98 Second Edition.  Both 98 First Edition and Millenniuum are buggy.  I've tried all three.  Also, if you do a clean format and full re-install, you should only have to do it once.  If you're getting I/O errors, then you've likely got a hardware problem.  Either bad CD media, bad CDROM drive, or HDD going bad, or any cabling connecting any of these.  Since you were inside the PC installing the RAM, you may have knocked loose a connector and not realized it.  It happens quite frequently.  Remove and reseat all the power and data cables and see if that helps.  You'll want to do this before you do a reformat and install.  If you installed Windows with a loose cable, some data corruption could have happened and fixing the loose cable won't make the problem go away.  Reseat, the reformat and reload the OS.  ||||reg||1
