Z||000024||N_Man||04-22-2001||01:42 PM||||LarryB<BR>i dont know if my BH6 is special or what but in my BIOS i can set the BUS speed to 126(1/4)N, that is the exact line, so infact i would be running the PCI bus at 31.5 and that will give me no problems with the system. Except for my AGP slot I can only set the multiplier to 1/1 or 2/3 so at 2/3 my AGP is running at 84MHz, definitly fast and probably the limiting factor on my overclocking.<BR>Also now that everything is running good again im gonna try all the chips in all the slots and see what i can come up with.  And as far as brand name I did buy MICRON memory, but the old stuff is generic, possibly the reason for its problems.  Finally the first thing in all this was to set my bus speed back to 100MHz.<P>btoth<BR>ive been told by at least 5 people that you can normally use different spped memory with other, but now im not sure i believe them.<P>buy a mac LOL what a joke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>But seriously windows is now running rock solid on the computer I havent been able to phaze it one bit, except for office 97 that just wont install, but im gonna see if a can try office 2000||||reg||1
Z||000025||Loki||04-22-2001||02:27 PM||||As for the different memory speeds..If you have 100mhz bus speed you can use 133..but if you have 133 you cant use 100<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000026||Cameron||04-23-2001||02:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>As for the different memory speeds..If you have 100mhz bus speed you can use 133..but if you have 133 you cant use 100</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry, but your data on ram is inaccurate.  If you have a 133 mhz bus you can use 100 mhz ram.  But if you have a 100 mhz bus you can't use 133mhz ram.  The computer bus is "smart" and can step it's speed down where the ram isn't.<P><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||DISenchanted||04-23-2001||04:26 AM||||Did he just say "Windows" and "rock solid" in  the same sentence?  Then follow it by laughing at a "Mac"?  Someone needs to rethink their statements...<P>DISenchanted||||reg||5
Z||000028||LarryB||04-23-2001||07:11 PM||||Uh, no.<P>Loki had it right in the first place.<P>PC-100 memory is only certified for use up to 100MHz FSB, PC-133 is certified for use @ 133MHz FSB. So, you can use PC133 memory @100MHz.  Good quality PC100 memory may work at 133MHz but its not guaranteed by any means.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cameron:<BR><B> Sorry, but your data on ram is inaccurate.  If you have a 133 mhz bus you can use 100 mhz ram.  But if you have a 100 mhz bus you can't use 133mhz ram.  The computer bus is "smart" and can step it's speed down where the ram isn't.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||9
